  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-506695</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam in Cambodia is working to support forest dependent communities who have conserved and managed communal forest resources. The communities supported are community forestries and community protected areas. In order to motivate and give incentive to communities, Oxfam in Cambodia recently provided community based carbon measurement to community forestry and community protected areas management committees. The objectives of the training include to raise awareness of community on how important of their roles in contributing to national climate change strategies especially carbon neutrality plan and at the same time attract attentions from government to give more supports to them through the government climate actions. Through this initiative, Oxfam intents to move on the next steps which supporting the forest dependent communities to be able access to carbon financing programs that including carbon credit. To start with, Oxfam in Cambodia would engage a service provider to conduct feasibility study on some CF and CPA sites.</narrative>
  </description>
